# client/configs/ai-apks.list
# Minimal container runtime (Docker) needed to run the on-demand Ollama GPU
# container. These are LAZY-LOADED (like pentest-lazy.list): the .apk files are
# baked into the ISO's on-disk repository so ai-extra.sh can install them OFFLINE
# on demand, but they are NOT written to /etc/apk/world - they must never extract
# into the 4G tmpfs root at boot.
#
# docker runs individually; together with the ollama squashfs it is a several-GB
# disk footprint that would first blow boot RAM and then sit unused. It loads
# only when /usr/local/bin/ai-extra.sh runs.
#
# Source of truth: /etc/ai-apks.list (copied verbatim by build pipelines).
docker
docker-cli
docker-cli-buildx
docker-cli-compose